# rack_id  site_label  node1 node2 ... nodeN
#
# One line per rack. A rack = one NVLink domain = the unit an llmb-run job
# occupies. Generated by bin/interview.sh; regenerate any time with
# docs/gen-inventory-from-slurm.sh.
#
# site_label is free-form (a physical rack tag, or '-'). It is only used for
# grouping sanity checks and reports.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE AUTHORITY on rack membership. Never derive membership by
# arithmetic on node names: node numbering inside a rack is frequently NOT
# contiguous, and a "-[01-18]" style assumption silently builds a wrong
# --nodelist, which presents as jobs pending forever with no error.
#
# Example - 2 racks of 18 trays, with non-contiguous tray numbering:
rack01 A1 rack01-11 rack01-12 rack01-13 rack01-14 rack01-15 rack01-16 rack01-17 rack01-18 rack01-28 rack01-29 rack01-30 rack01-31 rack01-32 rack01-33 rack01-34 rack01-35 rack01-36 rack01-37
rack02 A2 rack02-11 rack02-12 rack02-13 rack02-14 rack02-15 rack02-16 rack02-17 rack02-18 rack02-28 rack02-29 rack02-30 rack02-31 rack02-32 rack02-33 rack02-34 rack02-35 rack02-36 rack02-37
